msgid "OptaPlanner - Using AI to optimize a schedule with OptaPlanner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide walks you through the process of creating a Quarkus application\n"
"with https://www.optaplanner.org/[OptaPlanner]'s constraint solving "
"Artificial Intelligence (AI)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you will build"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You will build a REST application that optimizes a school timetable for "
"students and teachers:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your service will assign `Lesson` instances to `Timeslot` and `Room` "
"instances automatically\n"
"by using AI to adhere to hard and soft scheduling _constraints_, such as the "
"following examples:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A room can have at most one lesson at the same time."
msgstr ""

msgid "A teacher can teach at most one lesson at the same time."
msgstr ""

msgid "A student can attend at most one lesson at the same time."
msgstr ""

msgid "A teacher prefers to teach all lessons in the same room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A teacher prefers to teach sequential lessons and dislikes gaps between "
"lessons."
msgstr ""

msgid "A student dislikes sequential lessons on the same subject."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mathematically speaking, school timetabling is an _NP-hard_ problem.\n"
"This means it is difficult to scale.\n"
"Simply brute force iterating through all possible combinations takes "
"millions of years\n"
"for a non-trivial dataset, even on a supercomputer.\n"
"Luckily, AI constraint solvers such as OptaPlanner have advanced algorithms\n"
"that deliver a near-optimal solution in a reasonable amount of time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the completed example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in {quickstarts-tree-url}/optaplanner-quickstart[the "
"`optaplanner-quickstart` directory]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly {prerequisites-time}"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 11+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid "The build file and the dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use https://code.quarkus.io/[code.quarkus.io] to generate an application\n"
"with the following extensions, for Maven or Gradle:"
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy Reactive (`quarkus-resteasy-reactive`)"
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy Reactive Jackson (`quarkus-resteasy-reactive-jackson`)"
msgstr ""

msgid "OptaPlanner (`optaplanner-quarkus`)"
msgstr ""

msgid "OptaPlanner Jackson (`optaplanner-quarkus-jackson`)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Alternatively, generate it from the command line:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `--gradle` or `--gradle-kotlin-dsl` "
"option."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"_For more information about how to install the Quarkus CLI and use it, "
"please refer to xref:cli-tooling.adoc[the Quarkus CLI guide]._"
msgstr ""

msgid "Maven"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `-DbuildTool=gradle` or `-DbuildTool="
"gradle-kotlin-dsl` option."
msgstr ""

msgid "This will include the following dependencies in your build file:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Model the domain objects"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your goal is to assign each lesson to a time slot and a room.\n"
"You will create these classes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Timeslot"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Timeslot` class represents a time interval when lessons are taught,\n"
"for example, `Monday 10:30 - 11:30` or `Tuesday 13:30 - 14:30`.\n"
"For simplicity's sake, all time slots have the same duration\n"
"and there are no time slots during lunch or other breaks."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A time slot has no date, because a high school schedule just repeats every "
"week.\n"
"So there is no need for https://docs.optaplanner.org/latestFinal/optaplanner-"
"docs/html_single/index.html#continuousPlanning[continuous planning]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/domain/Timeslot.java` class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Because no `Timeslot` instances change during solving, a `Timeslot` is "
"called a _problem fact_.\n"
"Such classes do not require any OptaPlanner specific annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Notice the `toString()` method keeps the output short,\n"
"so it is easier to read OptaPlanner's `DEBUG` or `TRACE` log, as shown later."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "Room"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Room` class represents a location where lessons are taught,\n"
"for example, `Room A` or `Room B`.\n"
"For simplicity's sake, all rooms are without capacity limits\n"
"and they can accommodate all lessons."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/domain/Room.java` class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`Room` instances do not change during solving, so `Room` is also a _problem "
"fact_."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lesson"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"During a lesson, represented by the `Lesson` class,\n"
"a teacher teaches a subject to a group of students,\n"
"for example, `Math by A.Turing for 9th grade` or `Chemistry by M.Curie for "
"10th grade`.\n"
"If a subject is taught multiple times per week by the same teacher to the "
"same student group,\n"
"there are multiple `Lesson` instances that are only distinguishable by `id`.\n"
"For example, the 9th grade has six math lessons a week."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"During solving, OptaPlanner changes the `timeslot` and `room` fields of the "
"`Lesson` class,\n"
"to assign each lesson to a time slot and a room.\n"
"Because OptaPlanner changes these fields, `Lesson` is a _planning entity_:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most of the fields in the previous diagram contain input data, except for "
"the orange fields:\n"
"A lesson's `timeslot` and `room` fields are unassigned (`null`) in the input "
"data\n"
"and assigned (not `null`) in the output data.\n"
"OptaPlanner changes these fields during solving.\n"
"Such fields are called planning variables.\n"
"In order for OptaPlanner to recognize them,\n"
"both the `timeslot` and `room` fields require an `@PlanningVariable` "
"annotation.\n"
"Their containing class, `Lesson`, requires an `@PlanningEntity` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/domain/Lesson.java` class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Lesson` class has an `@PlanningEntity` annotation,\n"
"so OptaPlanner knows that this class changes during solving\n"
"because it contains one or more planning variables."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `timeslot` field has an `@PlanningVariable` annotation,\n"
"so OptaPlanner knows that it can change its value.\n"
"In order to find potential `Timeslot` instances to assign to this field,\n"
"OptaPlanner uses the `valueRangeProviderRefs` property to connect to a value "
"range provider\n"
"(explained later) that provides a `List<Timeslot>` to pick from."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `room` field also has an `@PlanningVariable` annotation, for the same "
"reasons."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Determining the `@PlanningVariable` fields for an arbitrary constraint "
"solving use case\n"
"is often challenging the first time.\n"
"Read https://docs.optaplanner.org/latestFinal/optaplanner-docs/html_single/"
"index.html#domainModelingGuide[the domain modeling guidelines]\n"
"to avoid common pitfalls."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define the constraints and calculate the score"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A _score_ represents the quality of a specific solution.\n"
"The higher, the better.\n"
"OptaPlanner looks for the best solution, which is the solution with the "
"highest score found in the available time.\n"
"It might be the _optimal_ solution."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Because this use case has hard and soft constraints,\n"
"use the `HardSoftScore` class to represent the score:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hard constraints must not be broken. For example: _A room can have at most "
"one lesson at the same time._"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Soft constraints should not be broken. For example: _A teacher prefers to "
"teach in a single room._"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hard constraints are weighted against other hard constraints.\n"
"Soft constraints are weighted too, against other soft constraints.\n"
"*Hard constraints always outweigh soft constraints*, regardless of their "
"respective weights."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To calculate the score, you could implement an `EasyScoreCalculator` class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Unfortunately **that does not scale well**, because it is non-incremental:\n"
"every time a lesson is assigned to a different time slot or room,\n"
"all lessons are re-evaluated to calculate the new score."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead, create a `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/solver/"
"TimeTableConstraintProvider.java` class\n"
"to perform incremental score calculation.\n"
"It uses OptaPlanner's ConstraintStream API which is inspired by Java Streams "
"and SQL:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `ConstraintProvider` scales an order of magnitude better than the "
"`EasyScoreCalculator`: __O__(n) instead of __O__(n²)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gather the domain objects in a planning solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A `TimeTable` wraps all `Timeslot`, `Room`, and `Lesson` instances of a "
"single dataset.\n"
"Furthermore, because it contains all lessons, each with a specific planning "
"variable state,\n"
"it is a _planning solution_ and it has a score:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If lessons are still unassigned, then it is an _uninitialized_ solution,\n"
"for example, a solution with the score `-4init/0hard/0soft`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If it breaks hard constraints, then it is an _infeasible_ solution,\n"
"for example, a solution with the score `-2hard/-3soft`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If it adheres to all hard constraints, then it is a _feasible_ solution,\n"
"for example, a solution with the score `0hard/-7soft`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/domain/TimeTable.java` class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `TimeTable` class has an `@PlanningSolution` annotation,\n"
"so OptaPlanner knows that this class contains all the input and output data."
msgstr ""

msgid "Specifically, this class is the input of the problem:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A `timeslotList` field with all time slots"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is a list of problem facts, because they do not change during solving."
msgstr ""

msgid "A `roomList` field with all rooms"
msgstr ""

msgid "A `lessonList` field with all lessons"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is a list of planning entities, because they change during solving."
msgstr ""

msgid "Of each `Lesson`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The values of the `timeslot` and `room` fields are typically still `null`, "
"so unassigned.\n"
"They are planning variables."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The other fields, such as `subject`, `teacher` and `studentGroup`, are "
"filled in.\n"
"These fields are problem properties."
msgstr ""

msgid "However, this class is also the output of the solution:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A `lessonList` field for which each `Lesson` instance has non-null "
"`timeslot` and `room` fields after solving"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A `score` field that represents the quality of the output solution, for "
"example, `0hard/-5soft`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The value range providers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `timeslotList` field is a value range provider.\n"
"It holds the `Timeslot` instances which OptaPlanner can pick from to assign "
"to the `timeslot` field of `Lesson` instances.\n"
"The `timeslotList` field has an `@ValueRangeProvider` annotation to connect "
"the `@PlanningVariable` with the `@ValueRangeProvider`,\n"
"by matching the value of the `id` property with the value of the "
"`valueRangeProviderRefs` property of the `@PlanningVariable` annotation in "
"the `Lesson` class."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Following the same logic, the `roomList` field also has an "
"`@ValueRangeProvider` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid "The problem fact and planning entity properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Furthermore, OptaPlanner needs to know which `Lesson` instances it can "
"change\n"
"as well as how to retrieve the `Timeslot` and `Room` instances used for "
"score calculation\n"
"by your `TimeTableConstraintProvider`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `timeslotList` and `roomList` fields have an "
"`@ProblemFactCollectionProperty` annotation,\n"
"so your `TimeTableConstraintProvider` can select _from_ those instances."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `lessonList` has an `@PlanningEntityCollectionProperty` annotation,\n"
"so OptaPlanner can change them during solving\n"
"and your `TimeTableConstraintProvider` can select _from_ those too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create the solver service"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now you are ready to put everything together and create a REST service.\n"
"But solving planning problems on REST threads causes HTTP timeout issues.\n"
"Therefore, the Quarkus extension injects a `SolverManager` instance,\n"
"which runs solvers in a separate thread pool\n"
"and can solve multiple datasets in parallel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/optaplanner/rest/TimeTableResource.java` "
"class:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For simplicity's sake, this initial implementation waits for the solver to "
"finish,\n"
"which can still cause an HTTP timeout.\n"
"The _complete_ implementation avoids HTTP timeouts much more elegantly."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set the termination time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Without a termination setting or a termination event, the solver runs "
"forever.\n"
"To avoid that, limit the solving time to five seconds.\n"
"That is short enough to avoid the HTTP timeout."
msgstr ""

